Setup signing:

    Edit your private/local "~/.gradle/gradle.properties" and add a line:

        Sshd4a.properties=/path/to/Sshd4a.properties

    Edit/create the file "/path/to/Sshd4a.properties":

        sign.storeFile=/path/to/myKeystore.jks
        sign.storePassword=myPass
        sign.keyAlias=myAlias
        sign.keyPassword=myPass

    Alternatively the properties file can be passed directly on the Gradle
    command line (equivalent to the "gradle.properties" entry above; this is
    what CI does):

        ./gradlew assembleRelease -PSshd4a.properties=/path/to/Sshd4a.properties

    "app/build.gradle" applies the release signing configuration only when
    that property points to an existing properties file with content.
    Otherwise the release APK is built UNSIGNED:

        Keystore properties file not found. No signing configuration will be applied.

    GitHub Actions (".github/workflows/build-apk.yml") does this automatically
    from the repository secrets:

        KEYSTORE_BASE64     base64 of the keystore, e.g.  base64 -w0 myKeystore.jks
        KEYSTORE_PASSWORD   keystore password
        KEY_ALIAS           key alias
        KEY_PASSWORD        key password

    The workflow decodes the keystore to "$RUNNER_TEMP/keystore.jks", writes a
    "sign.*" properties file and passes it via "-PSshd4a.properties". When the
    secrets are not set (e.g. pull requests from forks) the release APK stays
    unsigned and the build still succeeds.

    Keep the keystore, its passwords and the properties file out of the repo.
